1
00:00:07,913 --> 00:00:13,186
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,421 --> 00:00:15,364
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:16,814 --> 00:00:17,985
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

4
00:00:18,010 --> 00:00:18,890
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

5
00:00:18,915 --> 00:00:22,271
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

6
00:00:23,252 --> 00:00:27,330
Hassan Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه, as we mentioned previously

7
00:00:27,987 --> 00:00:33,640
was, what we could call him the head of the media effort of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

8
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:44,520
he was the one who would respond back with poetry against the poets of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and the other enemies of Islam.

9
00:00:45,021 --> 00:00:49,370
So, Hassan Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه said a lot of lines of poetry,

10
00:00:49,791 --> 00:00:55,267
 talking about the treachery and the betrayal of those tribes in Najd(نجد),

11
00:00:55,624 --> 00:01:00,009
who killed the 70 Qurr'ah(قرا), the teachers of Qur'an.

12
00:01:00,879 --> 00:01:05,967
 Obviously, translating lines of poetry into different language, you lose the beauty of it

13
00:01:06,028 --> 00:01:11,014
 but he has some wonderful lines of poetry talking about those events.

14
00:01:12,323 --> 00:01:16,283
Az-Zubair Bin Awwam رضي الله عنه and I also think I mentioned this before,

15
00:01:16,323 --> 00:01:19,278
he would name his children after the Shuhadaa(شهداء).

16
00:01:19,584 --> 00:01:23,904
So he named two of his sons, after two of the Shuhadaa(شهداء) in Bier Maoona(بئر ماعونه).

17
00:01:24,106 --> 00:01:26,619
One of them was Urwa(عروة) and the other one was Al-Mundhir(المنذر).

18
00:01:27,025 --> 00:01:30,061
So, two of the sons of Az-Zubair(الزبير) were named after Shuhadaa(شهداء).

19
00:01:30,702 --> 00:01:32,439
It says that Zubair(زبير) and Talha(طلحه) were friends,

20
00:01:33,096 --> 00:01:35,504
and both of them belong to the group of 10

21
00:01:35,933 --> 00:01:37,775
who were given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

22
00:01:38,707 --> 00:01:42,781
Talha(طلحه), he would name his sons, after the Ambiyaa(أنبياء),

23
00:01:43,233 --> 00:01:45,351
and Zubair(زبير) would name them, after the Shuhadaa(شهداء).

24
00:01:46,223 --> 00:01:52,038
Rasool Allah ﷺ also during that period of time got married to Zainab Bint Khuzaimah(زينب بنت خزيمه)

25
00:01:52,418 --> 00:01:57,083
and she is called Umm-Ul-Masakeen(ام المساكين) the mother of the poor.

26
00:01:57,619 --> 00:02:05,334
Why.? Because he used to take care of the poor and give them food, give them money, she was very caring of the poor.

27
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,168
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ married her.

28
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:10,860
She was the wife of Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش), who was killed in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

29
00:02:11,667 --> 00:02:18,088
And we can see here in the marriages of Rasool Allah ﷺ an element of social welfare

30
00:02:18,269 --> 00:02:20,678
Rasool Allah ﷺ taking care of his followers.

31
00:02:21,417 --> 00:02:24,545
So, after Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) died as a Shaheed(شهيد).

32
00:02:24,625 --> 00:02:28,357
Rasool Allah ﷺ marries his wife and takes care of her.

33
00:02:28,677 --> 00:02:31,543
And we can see that throughout the marriages of Rasool Allah ﷺ

34
00:02:31,583 --> 00:02:33,721
and also in many of the marriages of the Sahabah(صحابه),

35
00:02:33,761 --> 00:02:37,997
they didn't want to leave any woman behind without a husband, without a family.

36
00:02:38,855 --> 00:02:43,457
And that was part of the reason or the Hikmah(حكمة) behind polygamy.

37
00:02:44,008 --> 00:02:49,294
One should not think that it's solely for the purpose of satisfying one desires,

38
00:02:49,374 --> 00:02:57,013
 there are some other aspects to marriage, bring up a Muslim family, taking care of one another.

39
00:02:57,068 --> 00:02:58,814
  وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَكُمْ مَوَدَّةً وَرَحْمَةً ۚ

40
00:02:58,854 --> 00:03:00,025
As Allahعَزّوجَلّ says.

41
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:03,195
Rasool Allah ﷺ also got married to Ummo Salamah(ام سلمه).

42
00:03:03,651 --> 00:03:08,770
Ummo Salamah رضي الله عنها is from Quraish(قريش), she's from Bannu Makhzoom(بنو مخزوم), an important family in Quraish(قريش),

43
00:03:09,238 --> 00:03:11,370
 this is the family of Khalid Bin Waleed(خالد بن وليد), by the way.

44
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:17,270
And her husband, Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) was one of the early Sahabah(صحابه),

45
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:20,794
he made Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(حبشه) and he also made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina,

46
00:03:20,876 --> 00:03:22,789
so he's one of those who made the two Hijrah(هجرة)'s

47
00:03:23,483 --> 00:03:26,286
and he fought in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) and he was injured.

48
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,791
Now his injury was starting to heal,

49
00:03:28,831 --> 00:03:31,767
Rasool Allah ﷺ sends him on another mission,

50
00:03:32,251 --> 00:03:39,166
and during that mission, his injury starts all over again, and he ends up dying.

51
00:03:39,687 --> 00:03:45,435
Now, before that Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) has a conversation with his wife.

52
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,761
He tells her, if a husband dies

53
00:03:50,516 --> 00:03:52,475
and his wife does not get married after him,

54
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,629
they would be brought together again in Jannah(جنة).

55
00:03:56,024 --> 00:03:57,966
If both of them are destined to go to Jannah(جنة).

56
00:03:58,528 --> 00:04:02,852
So, Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) told his wife, How about, we make an agreement,

57
00:04:03,252 --> 00:04:06,641
If I die, you do not get married, if you die I don't get married.

58
00:04:07,030 --> 00:04:09,204
She said: Fine, I agree.

59
00:04:09,569 --> 00:04:11,386
He then told her: No.

60
00:04:11,802 --> 00:04:13,540
I asked Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

61
00:04:13,873 --> 00:04:17,969
 If I die then He replaces me with somebody better,

62
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:21,359
who will marry you and will not harm you or hurt you.

63
00:04:22,516 --> 00:04:25,398
Ummo Salamah(أم سلمه) would then say and who is better than Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه).

64
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:28,635
Who will I find in the world, better than Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه).

65
00:04:29,121 --> 00:04:31,515
So this shows you that they had a very good relationship.

66
00:04:31,936 --> 00:04:37,150
When he died she went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) is dead.

67
00:04:37,875 --> 00:04:42,769
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Say, O Allah forgive me and forgive him

68
00:04:43,325 --> 00:04:45,280
and replace me with somebody better.

69
00:04:45,757 --> 00:04:47,407
وَاعقُبْنِيْ مِنْهُ عُقْبَهْ حَسَنَهْ

70
00:04:47,447 --> 00:04:48,915
Or give me something that is better.

71
00:04:49,571 --> 00:04:50,653
And she made that Dua(دُعَا),

72
00:04:51,264 --> 00:04:54,955
Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه proposed marriage, she refused,

73
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:58,456
Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) proposes marriage, she refuses.

74
00:04:59,891 --> 00:05:01,528
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ

75
00:05:01,973 --> 00:05:03,417
اَرْسَلَ إلَيْهَا يَخْطبُهَا

76
00:05:03,457 --> 00:05:06,588
He proposed marriage, she said: Marhaba(مرحبا), Welcome.

77
00:05:07,439 --> 00:05:09,195
But tell Rasool Allah ﷺ

78
00:05:09,856 --> 00:05:13,489
اِنِّيْ غَيْرَة وَ اِنِّيْ مَسْبِيَّه وَلَيْسَ اَحَدٌ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآئي شَهَدْ

79
00:05:14,455 --> 00:05:17,153
 Tell Rasool Allah ﷺ that I am a jealous woman,

80
00:05:17,768 --> 00:05:21,888
and I have kids, young kids, and none of my Walii(ولي) are present.

81
00:05:22,731 --> 00:05:26,028
So I agree, but let Rasool Allah ﷺ know my condition

82
00:05:26,707 --> 00:05:29,284
I'm a very jealous woman and Rasool Allah ﷺ is already married.

83
00:05:30,646 --> 00:05:33,367
And I have kids and these kids are gonna be a burden on him

84
00:05:33,744 --> 00:05:37,159
and then none of my Wallii(ولي) are here to marry me to you.

85
00:05:37,478 --> 00:05:38,780
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

86
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:43,708
اَمَّا قَوْلُكِ اِنِيْ مُسْبِيَة فَاِنَّ الله سَيَكفيْكِ صبْيَانَكْ

87
00:05:44,562 --> 00:05:47,643
You said that you have children, Allahعَزّوجَلّ will take care of those kids.

88
00:05:48,283 --> 00:05:52,386
وَاَمَّا قَوْلُكِ اِنَّيْ غَيْرَة فَسَأدعُو الله اَنْ يَذْهَبَ غَيْرَتُكِ

89
00:05:52,948 --> 00:05:57,122
You said that you are jealous I'm gonna ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to take that jealousy away.

90
00:05:57,944 --> 00:06:01,520
وَاَمَّا الْاَوْلِيَآءْ  فَلَيْسَ اَحَدُ مِّنْهُمْ اِلَّا سَيَرْضَى بِي

91
00:06:01,886 --> 00:06:03,599
And the Wallii(ولي)'s who are absent,

92
00:06:03,798 --> 00:06:09,324
none of them will refuse to marry you to me, all of them will be happy that you would marry me.

93
00:06:10,442 --> 00:06:12,688
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ marries Ummo Salamah(ام سلمه).

94
00:06:12,728 --> 00:06:14,951
In another narration it said that she told him,

95
00:06:15,295 --> 00:06:19,006
I mean, I agree, but I'm an old woman, I'm getting old.

96
00:06:19,399 --> 00:06:20,641
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

97
00:06:21,024 --> 00:06:23,101
If you are old I'm older than you.

98
00:06:24,377 --> 00:06:29,958
And I think this also shows you, the intention of Rasool Allah ﷺ, in his marriage from Ummo Salamah رضي الله عنها.

99
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:34,346
And I talked about this, in my series on the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ in Makkah.

100
00:06:34,964 --> 00:06:39,159
We talked about his marriages and the objectives that his marriages would serve.

101
00:06:39,674 --> 00:06:44,443
So, the marriages of Rasool Allah ﷺ were marriages for the sake of the Ummah(امة), for the sake of the religion.

102
00:06:45,585 --> 00:06:50,042
Ummo Salamah رضي الله عنها, narrated 338 Ahadith(احاديث),

103
00:06:50,609 --> 00:06:53,466
very important to Ahadith(احاديث), some in Bukhari(بخاريْ), some in Muslim(مسلم).

104
00:06:54,273 --> 00:06:59,081
And she conveyed to us this knowledge from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

105
00:06:59,622 --> 00:07:05,609
So, that is one of the reasons, why Allahعَزّوجَلّ destined Rasool Allah ﷺ to marry Ummo Salamahرضي الله عنها

106
00:07:05,674 --> 00:07:11,068
because everything happened, according to the destiny of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and His plan for this religion.

107
00:07:12,166 --> 00:07:14,313
So, his marriage to Ayesha(عائشه) was a Barakah(بركة) for us.

108
00:07:14,659 --> 00:07:16,862
His marriage with Zainab(زينب) was a Barakah(بركة) for us.

109
00:07:16,942 --> 00:07:19,384
His marriage to Khadijah(خديجه) was a Barakah(بركة) for us.

110
00:07:19,424 --> 00:07:21,266
His marriage to Ummo Salamah(ام سلمه) was a Barakah(بركة) for us.

111
00:07:21,306 --> 00:07:24,599
All of his marriages served a purpose in Islam, for us.

112
00:07:26,006 --> 00:07:28,814
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ married her and

113
00:07:29,292 --> 00:07:33,584
he said that I'm going to give you a furniture equal to that which I gave to Zainab(زينب).

114
00:07:34,479 --> 00:07:35,873
So, what was this furniture?

115
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:42,168
Did they go to what are those famous, furniture places IKEA, whatever

116
00:07:42,221 --> 00:07:53,037
and buy new set, furniture, 10's of thousands of dollars worth of furniture for the newly wed couple.

117
00:07:53,695 --> 00:07:57,005
What was the furniture that Rasool Allah ﷺ got for Ummo Salamah(ام سلمه)?

118
00:07:58,045 --> 00:08:00,719
Keep in mind here we're talking about the best of mankind.

119
00:08:01,354 --> 00:08:10,600
The one, who, if he wanted he could have spent on his wives, all the money that he could.

120
00:08:11,005 --> 00:08:16,935
Rasool Allah ﷺ was getting money from all of these Ghazawaat(غزوات) Ghameena(غنيمه) that was coming in,

121
00:08:16,964 --> 00:08:22,194
 Rasool Allah ﷺ could have spent that lavishly on his wives and nobody would have complained.

122
00:08:22,257 --> 00:08:26,103
I mean he's the Messenger of Allah, he deserves to have his family live the best life,

123
00:08:26,701 --> 00:08:28,568
who would have dare to complain about that.

124
00:08:29,415 --> 00:08:34,920
But Rasool Allah ﷺ was setting an example for his Ummah(امة) in Zuhud(زهد), austerity.

125
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:36,560
 He said;

126
00:08:36,923 --> 00:08:40,233
اَمَا اِنِّيْ لَا اَنْقُصكِ مِمَّا اَعْطَيْتُ فُلَانَ

127
00:08:40,757 --> 00:08:45,025
يَحْيَيْنْ وَ جَرَّتَيْنْ وِسادَةٌ مِنْ أَدَمٍ حَشْوُها لِيفٌ

128
00:08:45,856 --> 00:08:49,372
I will give you a no less than what I gave so and so.

129
00:08:49,966 --> 00:08:53,836
I gave her two stone Mills, two clay jars

130
00:08:54,313 --> 00:08:59,902
and a pillow stuffed with leaf, leaf is palm leaves.

131
00:09:00,830 --> 00:09:07,560
That was the furniture two stone Mills, two clay jars and a pillow, that was it.

132
00:09:07,811 --> 00:09:12,279
That was the furniture that Rasool Allah ﷺ bought for Ummo Salamah رضي الله عنها, very simple life.

133
00:09:13,886 --> 00:09:17,500
And he spent three days with her, when he got married to her.

134
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:18,858
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

135
00:09:19,194 --> 00:09:21,383
لِلْبِكْرِ سَبْعْ وَللثَيِّبْ ثَلَاثْ

136
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:23,835
For a person who was married to more than one women.

137
00:09:24,287 --> 00:09:29,697
As soon as he gets married to the second wife or the third or the fourth.

138
00:09:30,162 --> 00:09:33,966
If she is a virgin, then he spends seven days with her.

139
00:09:34,294 --> 00:09:39,267
If she is widowed or divorced then he spends three days with her,

140
00:09:39,307 --> 00:09:43,883
 so since Ummo Salamah(ام سلمه) is a widow Rasool Allah ﷺ spent three days with her.

141
00:09:44,278 --> 00:09:48,041
Also during that year, Al-Hassan Bin Ali Bin Abi Talib(الحسن بن علي بن ابي طالب) was born.

142
00:09:48,731 --> 00:09:52,573
When he was born, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) brought to Rasool Allah ﷺ, the good news

143
00:09:52,892 --> 00:09:54,578
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What did he name him?

144
00:09:54,618 --> 00:09:56,035
He said, we named him Harb(حرب),

145
00:09:56,358 --> 00:09:57,366
Harb(حرب) means war.

146
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:00,216
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No, he is Hassan(حسن).

147
00:10:00,629 --> 00:10:04,024
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not like these harsh names, Harb(حرب) and Stone and

148
00:10:04,327 --> 00:10:08,002
you have sakher(صخر) you have Harb(حرب), you've all of these tough names.

149
00:10:08,329 --> 00:10:09,790
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not like that

150
00:10:10,117 --> 00:10:12,622
and he changed the name from Harb(حرب) to Hassan(حسن).

151
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:15,236
Hassan(حسن) means nice beautiful, kind.

152
00:10:15,482 --> 00:10:17,895
 It has all of these pleasant meanings.

153
00:10:18,268 --> 00:10:23,698
This is the name that he chose for his grandson Al-Hassan Bin Ali رضي الله عنه.

154
00:10:23,742 --> 00:10:29,899
Also we see here that it is he, who named his grandson, Al-Hassan رضي الله عنه.

155
00:10:30,514 --> 00:10:33,484
He made Azaan(آذان) in his ear, according to the Hadith(حديث),

156
00:10:34,099 --> 00:10:36,630
he asked his mother Fatima(فاطمه) to shave his head

157
00:10:37,134 --> 00:10:41,536
and then weigh it and pay the equivalent weight in silver as Sadaqah(صدقه) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

158
00:10:41,869 --> 00:10:44,028
and also he made Aqeeqah(عقيقه) for him,

159
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:48,874
they slaughtered for him two sheep, that was Aqeeqah(عقيقه) of Al-Hassan رضي الله عنه.

160
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:56,064
We're talking here about various events that happened during the fourth year of Hijrah(هجرى), after the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

161
00:10:57,296 --> 00:11:03,333
Also during that time Rasool Allah ﷺ calls in, Zaid Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه and he tells him

162
00:11:03,567 --> 00:11:10,002
يَا زَيْدْ تَعَلَّمَ كِتَابَة يَهُوْدْ فَاِنِيْ واللَّهِ ما آمَنُ يَهودَ علَى كتابي

163
00:11:10,027 --> 00:11:15,104
O Zaid(زيد), Learn the Hebrew language because I cannot trust, the Jews.

164
00:11:15,714 --> 00:11:18,990
I don't trust them to read my letters for me, I don't trust them

165
00:11:19,244 --> 00:11:25,926
hiring any one of them to be my assistant to read the letters that I received from them or to write back to them.

166
00:11:26,257 --> 00:11:29,964
Since Rasool Allah ﷺ was illiterate, he had to have these assistance

167
00:11:30,388 --> 00:11:33,031
to write letters for him and to read the letters that he received.

168
00:11:33,535 --> 00:11:36,972
So, there was some correspondence between Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Jews.

169
00:11:37,873 --> 00:11:43,577
So, he wanted a Muslim to be responsible for writing those letters and reading them for him.

170
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:48,658
Zaid رضي الله عنه said that I learned the Hebrew language in 15 days.

171
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:53,560
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) learning a new foreign language in 15 days

172
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:58,902
that shows you the persistence and the hard work of the Sahabah رضي الله عنه,

173
00:11:59,765 --> 00:12:03,660
within 15 days, he was ready to go, he learned a foreign language.

174
00:12:04,025 --> 00:12:07,716
So probably for all of those brothers and sisters want to learn Arabic

175
00:12:07,756 --> 00:12:12,284
 you could learn a lot from the example of Zaid Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه,

176
00:12:12,915 --> 00:12:18,950
Zaid Bin Thabit(زيد بن ثابت) I mean, shouldn't take you years that you just plan to take the first step,

