369
00:25:54,798 --> 00:25:57,922
they were welcomed at Khaybar(خيبر) as heroes.

370
00:25:59,197 --> 00:26:05,395
And that's because they didn't want the Muslims to feel sorry for them or to laugh at their misfortune.

371
00:26:06,132 --> 00:26:11,368
When in reality it was a huge setback for them, giving up their houses and their lands.

372
00:26:11,734 --> 00:26:13,238
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an,

373
00:26:13,427 --> 00:26:15,652
يُخْرِبُونَ بُيُوتَهُمْ بِأَيْدِيهِمْ

374
00:26:15,797 --> 00:26:19,095
They were tearing down their houses, with their own hands and

375
00:26:19,146 --> 00:26:25,548
if you build your house and you lived in your house for years and you have all of these memories attached to this house.

376
00:26:25,898 --> 00:26:29,351
And then you're tearing it down with your own hand, how painful is that.?

377
00:26:30,073 --> 00:26:32,040
Some lessons from Ghazawat Bannu Nadhir(غزوة بنونضير),

378
00:26:32,091 --> 00:26:36,454
the entire Surah(سورة) was revealed talking about this Ghazwah(غزوة) it is Surah Tul Hashr(سورة الحشر)

379
00:26:36,898 --> 00:26:40,368
and Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) used to call it, the Surah(سورة) of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير).

380
00:26:41,134 --> 00:26:45,411
We'll go through some of the Ayaat(آيات) of this Surah(سورة) Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

381
00:26:45,754 --> 00:26:54,312
هُوَ الَّذِي أَخْرَجَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ لِأَوَّلِ الْحَشْرِ

382
00:26:55,092 --> 00:26:58,470
مَا ظَنَنْتُمْ أَنْ يَخْرُجُوا

383
00:26:58,984 --> 00:27:06,178
وَظَنُّوا أَنَّهُمْ مَانِعَتُهُمْ حُصُونُهُمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ

384
00:27:06,758 --> 00:27:11,129
فَأَتَاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَمْ يَحْتَسِبُوا

385
00:27:11,631 --> 00:27:14,757
وَقَذَفَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ الرُّعْبَ

386
00:27:15,139 --> 00:27:25,772
يُخْرِبُونَ بُيُوتَهُمْ بِأَيْدِيهِمْ وَأَيْدِي الْمُؤْمِنِينَ فَاعْتَبِرُوا يَا أُولِي الْأَبْصَارِ۝

387
00:27:26,815 --> 00:27:29,648
It is He, Who expelled the ones, who disbelieved

388
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:33,836
among the People of the Scripture from their homes, at the first gathering.

389
00:27:34,139 --> 00:27:36,313
You did not think they would leave

390
00:27:36,353 --> 00:27:40,980
 and they thought that there that their fortresses would protect them from Allah,

391
00:27:41,337 --> 00:27:51,284
so here Allah is saying that the expectations before on your side and on their side is that you can't drive them out.

392
00:27:51,977 --> 00:27:59,910
So, their fortresses were strong and powerful and they had plenty of fighters.

393
00:28:00,292 --> 00:28:03,422
They had a lot of wealth to finance war.

394
00:28:04,187 --> 00:28:09,779
So the expectation, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying that your expectation and their expectation was that they wouldn't leave.

395
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:13,328
So, the way it looked from the out start

396
00:28:13,975 --> 00:28:17,847
is that it will not be possible to drive them out nevertheless they did.

397
00:28:17,969 --> 00:28:19,532
 Why? Allah did so.

398
00:28:20,389 --> 00:28:21,313
هُوَ الَّذِي أَخْرَجَ

399
00:28:21,426 --> 00:28:23,695
He's the One, He is the One, Who expelled them.

400
00:28:24,376 --> 00:28:27,433
Allah says it is He, Who expelled the ones, who disbelieved

401
00:28:27,473 --> 00:28:30,934
among the People of the Scripture from their homes at the first gathering.

402
00:28:31,356 --> 00:28:36,611
You did not think they would leave, and they thought that their fortresses would protect them from Allah.

403
00:28:36,894 --> 00:28:40,228
And over here, Allah is talking about fortresses but this could apply to anything.

404
00:28:40,678 --> 00:28:45,147
I mean any nation or any superpower who thinks that their weapons,

405
00:28:45,207 --> 00:28:50,282
no matter what these weapons are can stand between them and the Qadar(قدر) of Allah are mistaken.

406
00:28:50,605 --> 00:28:55,788
Whether these weapons are nuclear bombs or aircraft carriers or powerful airplanes or

407
00:28:56,129 --> 00:29:00,315
bombs, whatever, huge army million of fighters.

408
00:29:00,725 --> 00:29:03,941
If Allahعَزّوجَلّ wants to defeat a nation, that nation will be defeated.

409
00:29:04,564 --> 00:29:10,418
No one can stand between Allahعَزّوجَلّ and giving victory to His servants.

410
00:29:11,768 --> 00:29:17,332
Then Allah says but the decree of Allah came upon them from where they had not expected.

411
00:29:17,833 --> 00:29:20,263
See, no matter how strong your army is

412
00:29:20,671 --> 00:29:24,451
no matter how well your preparations are, how good your training is,

413
00:29:25,257 --> 00:29:29,460
no matter how many types of weapons you have.

414
00:29:30,499 --> 00:29:32,077
There are always going to be some gaps,

415
00:29:32,755 --> 00:29:34,959
there are always going to be some points of weakness

416
00:29:35,527 --> 00:29:36,957
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ knows these.

417
00:29:37,084 --> 00:29:41,958
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ will attack the enemies of Allah, through these points of weakness.

418
00:29:42,542 --> 00:29:45,512
Now how did it happen with the people of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير)?

419
00:29:45,711 --> 00:29:46,915
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

420
00:29:47,520 --> 00:29:51,586
But the decree of Allah, came upon them, from where they had not expected

421
00:29:52,033 --> 00:29:54,733
and He cast terror into their hearts.

422
00:29:55,267 --> 00:29:59,195
This was the soldier of Allah عَزّوجَلّ that defeated Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير).

423
00:29:59,842 --> 00:30:00,712
Fear.

424
00:30:01,362 --> 00:30:02,501
They were horrified,

425
00:30:03,057 --> 00:30:06,049
Allahعَزّوجَلّ cast fear into their hearts.

426
00:30:06,803 --> 00:30:10,949
So, if the heart is terrified, it doesn't make a difference,

427
00:30:11,203 --> 00:30:14,726
what arms you have, or how well fortified you are.

428
00:30:15,883 --> 00:30:17,042
And that's why Ibn Qayyim(ابن قيم) says

429
00:30:17,082 --> 00:30:26,226
that the Romans and Persians had stronger bodies greater numbers and more arms than the Muslims had,

430
00:30:26,966 --> 00:30:30,949
but their hearts failed them when they needed the most.

431
00:30:32,042 --> 00:30:36,445
When the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم stood in battle, in front of the Romans and Persians,

432
00:30:37,100 --> 00:30:42,979
in terms of physical ability, they probably were not as strong as their opponents,

433
00:30:43,399 --> 00:30:47,519
 their training was definitely less, their numbers were definitely less

434
00:30:48,074 --> 00:30:53,597
and the arms assortment that the Sahabah(صحابه) had, was very limited compared to what their opponents had.

435
00:30:54,473 --> 00:30:58,829
However the Sahabah(صحابه) had Eeman(إيمان) and that Eeman(إيمان) made their heart steadfast,

436
00:30:59,265 --> 00:31:02,813
while the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ were attached to Duniya(دنيا)

437
00:31:03,070 --> 00:31:06,506
 and Allahعَزّوجَلّ cast fear in their hearts and they lost.

438
00:31:08,556 --> 00:31:13,534
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, So take warning, or people of vision.

439
00:31:14,710 --> 00:31:15,656
And then Allah says;

440
00:31:15,937 --> 00:31:23,823
وَلَوْلَا أَنْ كَتَبَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْجَلَاءَ لَعَذَّبَهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيَا ۖ

441
00:31:24,207 --> 00:31:28,796
 وَلَهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ عَذَابُ النَّارِ۝

442
00:31:29,181 --> 00:31:33,725
And if not, that Allah had the decreed for them evacuation

443
00:31:34,118 --> 00:31:36,557
He would have punished them, in this world

444
00:31:37,071 --> 00:31:39,849
and for them in the Hereafter is the punishment of fire.

445
00:31:40,193 --> 00:31:43,161
So, Allah is saying if, the people of Nadhir(نضير) didn't evacuate

446
00:31:43,376 --> 00:31:46,101
their punishment would have been execution, which is even worse.

447
00:31:46,565 --> 00:31:48,037
That would be the punishment in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

448
00:31:48,367 --> 00:31:50,826
and the punishment in the hereafter, would be even greater.

449
00:31:51,329 --> 00:31:57,388
ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ شَاقُّوا اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ

450
00:31:57,902 --> 00:32:06,226
وَمَنْ يُشَاقِّ اللَّهَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقَابِ۝

451
00:32:06,793 --> 00:32:09,606
That is because, they oppose Allah and His messenger

452
00:32:09,841 --> 00:32:14,710
and whoever opposes Allah then indeed, Allah is severe in penalty.

453
00:32:15,914 --> 00:32:19,371
So, this act Allahعَزّوجَلّ of defeating Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير)

454
00:32:20,395 --> 00:32:23,035
is because of their disbelief in Allah and His messengers.

455
00:32:24,013 --> 00:32:25,267
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is just,

456
00:32:25,370 --> 00:32:30,205
Allahعَزّوجَلّ did not punish them without deserving that punishment.

457
00:32:30,957 --> 00:32:34,445
Allahعَزّوجَلّ punish them because of standing against Islam.

458
00:32:35,279 --> 00:32:39,077
So, anyone who stands against Islam either an individual or a nation

459
00:32:39,724 --> 00:32:43,426
is calling upon themselves the Wrath of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

460
00:32:44,101 --> 00:32:44,893
Allah says;

461
00:32:44,951 --> 00:32:58,596
مَا قَطَعْتُمْ مِنْ لِينَةٍ أَوْ تَرَكْتُمُوهَا قَائِمَةً عَلَىٰ أُصُولِهَا فَبِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَلِيُخْزِيَ الْفَاسِقِينَ۝

462
00:32:59,962 --> 00:33:03,162
Whatever you have cut down of their palm trees,

463
00:33:03,202 --> 00:33:07,341
or left standing on their trunks, it was by the permission of Allah,

464
00:33:07,743 --> 00:33:11,713
and so He would disgrace the defiantly disobedient,

465
00:33:11,792 --> 00:33:18,417
so we go back to this issue of Muhammadﷺ, telling people not to destroy property and then he did it himself.

466
00:33:19,328 --> 00:33:22,682
First of all, this was done by the permission of Allah, according to this Ayah(آية)

467
00:33:23,342 --> 00:33:24,341
فَبِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ

468
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:26,138
It was by the permission of Allah.

469
00:33:26,470 --> 00:33:30,730
The ones that you cut down and the ones that remain that was by the permission of Allah.

470
00:33:31,143 --> 00:33:31,747
Why?

471
00:33:32,460 --> 00:33:34,345
وَلِيُخْزِيَ الْفَاسِقِينَ

472
00:33:34,385 --> 00:33:37,440
He would disgrace, the defiantly disobedient.

473
00:33:38,650 --> 00:33:45,336
Rasool Allah ﷺ has given instructions that trees should not be cut down

474
00:33:46,044 --> 00:33:49,510
women, children and old men should not be killed.

475
00:33:50,289 --> 00:33:54,454
He also said that monks, who are monasteries should not be killed.

476
00:33:55,497 --> 00:34:00,291
However, we find that with every one of these rules,

477
00:34:01,229 --> 00:34:04,604
there are incidents that go against the rule.

478
00:34:05,175 --> 00:34:07,145
So, here in Ghazwat(غزوة) Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير),

479
00:34:07,637 --> 00:34:14,138
Rasool Allah ﷺ has given orders to burn the palms down.

480
00:34:14,826 --> 00:34:18,304
So that is against the ruling of cutting down trees.

481
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:20,793
And then there's what is called Bayaat(بيآت)

482
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:25,309
and this is attacking at night, you attack the dwellings of people at night

483
00:34:26,024 --> 00:34:28,950
and the residents are killed.

484
00:34:29,391 --> 00:34:30,914
And Salmah Bin Aqwah(سلمة بن الاكوع) said;

485
00:34:30,954 --> 00:34:34,458
I myself participated in Bayaat(بيآت),

486
00:34:34,674 --> 00:34:38,514
 and I killed the residents of nine houses with my own hand.

487
00:34:38,986 --> 00:34:40,320
And this is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

488
00:34:40,837 --> 00:34:44,944
Now obviously here, you have men, women, children killed

489
00:34:45,024 --> 00:34:47,873
 because it's at night and they can be distinguished.

490
00:34:48,293 --> 00:34:52,984
So, this goes against the ruling of not killing women, children and old men.

491
00:34:53,571 --> 00:34:58,629
And then we also know that Rasool Allah ﷺ has ordered the execution of two women

492
00:34:59,439 --> 00:35:06,002
and one of those woman was, the woman who tried to poison Rasool Allah ﷺ a Yahoodi(يهودي) woman,

493
00:35:06,082 --> 00:35:08,383
 she was executed by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

494
00:35:08,933 --> 00:35:13,284
And we know that there were incidences where old men were killed.

495
00:35:14,036 --> 00:35:15,843
So, this goes against that ruling.

496
00:35:15,986 --> 00:35:21,730
And with the killing of monks, we know Salah-Ud-Din(صلاح الدين) for example

497
00:35:22,217 --> 00:35:25,732
would specifically even though, he was very tolerant with the Crusaders

498
00:35:26,228 --> 00:35:31,205
he would not let the members of the military religious orders

499
00:35:31,645 --> 00:35:36,690
such as the Templers or the hospitalors, he wouldn't let them go free, he would kill them.

500
00:35:37,164 --> 00:35:40,309
They were all executed, if they would land in his hands.

501
00:35:41,055 --> 00:35:43,885
And these were monks, these were religious men.

502
00:35:44,306 --> 00:35:47,758
So, this goes against the instruction of not killing monks.

503
00:35:47,798 --> 00:35:49,004
So what's going on here?

504
00:35:49,363 --> 00:35:52,246
How can we have this contradiction?

505
00:35:53,081 --> 00:35:54,633
The answer to that is the following.

506
00:35:55,355 --> 00:35:58,101
Islam is a tolerant religion.

507
00:35:58,685 --> 00:36:03,459
And the religion of Islam has laid down rules for engagement.

508
00:36:04,056 --> 00:36:07,522
There are rules that govern Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

509
00:36:08,240 --> 00:36:15,196
And these rules are to protect the rights of others and to protect the innocent life.

510
00:36:16,125 --> 00:36:22,260
However, whenever the enemy tries to take advantage of these rules

511
00:36:22,856 --> 00:36:26,281
and harm the Muslims these rules are suspended.

512
00:36:27,297 --> 00:36:32,067
So, if the enemy tries to take advantage of Muslims

513
00:36:32,425 --> 00:36:35,273
by using these restrictions against them.

514
00:36:35,995 --> 00:36:40,790
Then the Muslims are allowed to put those rules aside.

515
00:36:41,144 --> 00:36:42,064
To sum it up,

516
00:36:42,422 --> 00:36:47,477
Islam will not allow its tolerance to be used against it.

517
00:36:48,836 --> 00:36:55,542
So in this situation here Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered the cutting down of the trees of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير),

518
00:36:55,978 --> 00:36:59,700
 because Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير) were planning on a long siege.

519
00:37:00,192 --> 00:37:03,033
And they were depending on their palm trees

520
00:37:03,565 --> 00:37:08,029
while they deserved the punishment because of their betrayal,

521
00:37:08,358 --> 00:37:11,966
and because of their plotting to assassinate Rasool Allah ﷺ.

522
00:37:12,494 --> 00:37:19,002
So Rasool Allah ﷺ did not allow them to use his rules against the Muslims,

523
00:37:19,250 --> 00:37:22,724
and therefore he ordered the cutting down of trees.

524
00:37:23,898 --> 00:37:25,502
Allah عَزّوجَلّ says;

525
00:37:25,989 --> 00:37:33,817
وَمَا أَفَاءَ اللَّهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ مِنْهُمْ فَمَا أَوْجَفْتُمْ

526
00:37:34,729 --> 00:37:44,246
فَمَا أَوْجَفْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ خَيْلٍ وَلَا رِكَابٍ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ يُسَلِّطُ رُسُلَهُ

527
00:37:44,914 --> 00:37:52,142
وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ يُسَلِّطُ رُسُلَهُ عَلَىٰ مَنْ يَشَاءُ

528
00:37:52,741 --> 00:37:57,265
وَاللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ۝

529
00:37:58,096 --> 00:38:08,587
مَا أَفَاءَ اللَّهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْقُرَىٰ فَلِلَّهِ وَلِلرَّسُولِ وَلِذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ

530
00:38:09,333 --> 00:38:21,315
وَلِذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَالْيَتَامَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ كَيْ لَا يَكُونَ دُولَةً بَيْنَ الْأَغْنِيَاءِ مِنْكُمْ

531
00:38:21,925 --> 00:38:29,598
وَمَا آتَاكُمُ الرَّسُولُ فَخُذُوهُ وَمَا نَهَاكُمْ عَنْهُ فَانْتَهُوا

532
00:38:30,350 --> 00:38:36,179
وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقَابِ۝

533
00:38:36,987 --> 00:38:40,736
And what Allah restored of property to His messenger, from them

534
00:38:41,064 --> 00:38:45,838
you did not spare for it, in an expedition, any horses or camels.

535
00:38:46,437 --> 00:38:50,270
But Allah gives His messengers power over whom He wills

536
00:38:50,575 --> 00:38:52,465
and Allah is over all things competent.

537
00:38:53,035 --> 00:38:56,034
And what Allah restored to His messenger from the people of the towns

538
00:38:56,425 --> 00:38:59,714
it is for Allah and for the messenger and for his nearer relatives

539
00:38:59,834 --> 00:39:02,283
and the orphans and the stranded traveler,

540
00:39:02,635 --> 00:39:08,001
so that it will not be a perpetual distribution among the rich from among you

541
00:39:08,965 --> 00:39:11,165
and whatever the messenger has given you take

542
00:39:11,628 --> 00:39:14,738
and what he has forbidden you, refrain from

543
00:39:15,056 --> 00:39:17,909
and fear Allah indeed Allah is severe in penalty.

544
00:39:18,388 --> 00:39:20,821
So, this is talking about the rulings of Fae(فيئ).

545
00:39:21,266 --> 00:39:22,038
What is Fae(فيئ)?

546
00:39:22,440 --> 00:39:27,202
Ghaneemah(غنيمه) is the name given to spoils of war

547
00:39:27,806 --> 00:39:30,419
that are taken by the army after a fight.

548
00:39:31,353 --> 00:39:36,708
Fae(فيئ) are spoils of war that are taken by the army without a fight.

549
00:39:37,261 --> 00:39:41,212
Since no fighting occurred with Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير),

550
00:39:41,458 --> 00:39:46,254
since they surrendered and accepted to evacuate and leave behind their property

551
00:39:47,192 --> 00:39:50,395
except for what they can carry, since no fighting occurred.

552
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:56,331
 The ruling of what they leave behind is that it goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

553
00:39:57,043 --> 00:40:01,484
So the ruling of Ghaneemah(غنيمة), which is to split it into five portions

554
00:40:02,078 --> 00:40:05,078
four of those portions go to the fighters, does not apply here

555
00:40:05,502 --> 00:40:07,932
the entire thing goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ

556
00:40:07,972 --> 00:40:13,063
and he has authority to distribute it as he sees appropriate.

557
00:40:13,896 --> 00:40:16,653
So, these Ayaat(آيات) are talking about the ruling of Fae(فيئ).

558
00:40:17,601 --> 00:40:21,542
This was a new source of income for the Muslims

559
00:40:21,992 --> 00:40:26,579
and Ibn Is'haaq(اِبن إسحاق) says, they left their properties for the Messenger of Allah.

560
00:40:27,175 --> 00:40:30,508
These consisted of their palm trees and their farms,

561
00:40:31,140 --> 00:40:35,476
these became his personal property to dispose of, as he wished.

562
00:40:35,925 --> 00:40:37,388
So, it was up to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

563
00:40:38,150 --> 00:40:42,661
Rasool Ullah calls the Ansaar(أنصار), Al-Aos(الأوس) and Al-Khazraj(الخزرج), and he tells them.

564
00:40:42,967 --> 00:40:46,791
If you want I can split this money among you all,

565
00:40:46,831 --> 00:40:52,454
and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) continue living in your houses and working in your farms,

566
00:40:53,027 --> 00:40:58,739
or if you want I can distribute this money among the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) only.

567
00:40:59,451 --> 00:41:05,302
And they would leave your houses and not take any share from your harvest.

568
00:41:05,949 --> 00:41:09,963
Because if you go back earlier, we talked about that the Ansaar(أنصار) offered

569
00:41:10,716 --> 00:41:14,026
that they would share the harvest of their land with the Muhajireen(مهاجرين),

570
00:41:14,081 --> 00:41:16,101
 something they offered they didn't have to,

571
00:41:16,160 --> 00:41:18,692
but they were willing to share their harvest with the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون).

572
00:41:18,732 --> 00:41:20,047
So now Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

573
00:41:20,680 --> 00:41:24,436
it's up to you, I could distribute this among you all

574
00:41:24,786 --> 00:41:27,571
and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) continue living in your houses,

575
00:41:27,936 --> 00:41:32,159
 or they can move out and I'll give them this money of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير),

576
00:41:32,199 --> 00:41:34,563
so the Ansaar(أنصار) agreed and they said that

577
00:41:34,797 --> 00:41:37,484
you could distribute it to our brothers from Muhajiroon(مهاجرون),

578
00:41:37,782 --> 00:41:41,528
and if you want us to carry on giving them a share of our farms,

579
00:41:41,568 --> 00:41:43,058
we don't have a problem with that either.

580
00:41:43,647 --> 00:41:46,519
And this shows you the generosity of Al-Ansaar رضي الله عنهم.

581
00:41:46,836 --> 00:41:50,254
So, now Al-Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) moved into the houses of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير).

582
00:41:51,240 --> 00:41:54,598
So the difficult financial situation of Al-Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) was now lifted

583
00:41:55,038 --> 00:41:57,327
and their financial situation was improving.

584
00:41:57,635 --> 00:41:59,794
Now they have the houses of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير)

585
00:41:59,971 --> 00:42:02,398
and they also have the farms of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير),

586
00:42:02,649 --> 00:42:04,998
which were split among the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) only

587
00:42:05,312 --> 00:42:08,692
and only two men from Al-Ansaar(أنصار) were given a share

588
00:42:08,732 --> 00:42:10,981
and these two men were Sahal Bin Haneef(سهل بن حنيف) and Abu-Dujana(ابودجانه)

589
00:42:11,358 --> 00:42:14,737
because they complained of their poverty so, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave them some.

590
00:42:15,631 --> 00:42:19,428
Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) says, these were specifically for the Messenger of Allah

591
00:42:19,785 --> 00:42:23,148
he would set aside his family's expenses for a year

592
00:42:23,472 --> 00:42:26,456
and then whatever riding beast or weapons remained

593
00:42:26,664 --> 00:42:31,821
he would treat as military supplies to be used in the cause of Allah the Almighty and Glorious.

594
00:42:32,263 --> 00:42:36,190
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ now also, finally he had some wealth.

595
00:42:36,511 --> 00:42:42,327
 Before that he would live on gifts that he would get from the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

596
00:42:42,883 --> 00:42:45,335
Let's talk here about the livelihood of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

597
00:42:45,719 --> 00:42:48,025
We know that he started out his life as a shepherd.

598
00:42:48,232 --> 00:42:49,567
That was his first profession,

599
00:42:49,856 --> 00:42:52,736
number two, after that he worked as a businessman

600
00:42:53,177 --> 00:42:55,648
and he got to Khadeejah(خديجه) and he became her business manager,

601
00:42:55,688 --> 00:42:58,539
he would take care her business, for her.

602
00:42:59,028 --> 00:43:04,012
But when he was given the Risala(رسالة), Prophethood he stopped working.

603
00:43:04,663 --> 00:43:10,322
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ discontinued working as either a shepherd, or in business.

604
00:43:10,584 --> 00:43:14,544
Rasool Allah ﷺ devoted his entire time for Da'wah(دعوة).

605
00:43:15,012 --> 00:43:20,714
So, he would live off the money of Khadeejah رضي الله عنها and from his uncle, Abu Talib(ابو طالب),

606
00:43:21,315 --> 00:43:26,310
and then when he moved to Madina, the Ansaar(أنصار) would help Rasool Allah ﷺ,

607
00:43:26,350 --> 00:43:29,163
 obviously he's the Messenger of Allah, so he cannot accept Sadaqah(صدقه)

608
00:43:29,394 --> 00:43:30,948
but they would give him gifts.

609
00:43:31,361 --> 00:43:36,555
Now since this money of Fae(فيئ), all of it goes back to him

610
00:43:36,985 --> 00:43:40,633
he would take from it, his expenses for a year

611
00:43:41,200 --> 00:43:44,398
and then the rest he would spend in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

612
00:43:45,167 --> 00:43:46,279
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

613
00:43:46,375 --> 00:43:48,478
جُعِلَ رِزْقِيْ تَحْتَ ظِلْ رُمْحِيْ

614
00:43:48,807 --> 00:43:52,393
My provisions come from beneath my spear.

615
00:43:52,965 --> 00:43:56,873
So, my provisions come from fighting in the cause of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

616
00:43:56,937 --> 00:44:00,378
 that was the source of income for Rasool Allah ﷺ

617
00:44:00,735 --> 00:44:03,473
and he wasn't an employee, he didn't run a business

618
00:44:03,727 --> 00:44:07,917
all of his income would come from Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), from the spoils of war.

619
00:44:08,050 --> 00:44:09,478
جُعِلَ رِزْقِيْ تَحْتَ ظِلْ رُمْحِيْ

620
00:44:09,790 --> 00:44:12,476
My provisions come from under my spear.

621
00:44:13,286 --> 00:44:15,040
Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said;

622
00:44:15,080 --> 00:44:19,661
A man might donate to him, his palms or whatever else Allah might wish

623
00:44:19,788 --> 00:44:23,044
up to when Quraidha(قريظة) and Nadhir(نضير) were conquered for him

624
00:44:23,347 --> 00:44:25,756
there after he began giving it back.

625
00:44:25,883 --> 00:44:28,931
So, now finally Rasool Allah ﷺ has money to give back.

626
00:44:29,326 --> 00:44:31,780
Before that, he was taking now he's giving.

627
00:44:32,923 --> 00:44:36,814
Surat(سورة) Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير) also talks about the Munafiqoon(منافقون).

628
00:44:37,815 --> 00:44:40,983
These Munafiqeen(منافقين), who sent to Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير) and told them

629
00:44:41,060 --> 00:44:44,086
if you stay firm and resist, we will not give up on you,

630
00:44:44,166 --> 00:44:48,218
if you fight we'll fight along with you and if you're expelled, we will leave with you.

631
00:44:48,796 --> 00:44:50,351
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said about them;

632
00:44:51,128 --> 00:45:00,707
أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ نَافَقُوا يَقُولُونَ لِإِخْوَانِهِمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ

633
00:45:01,324 --> 00:45:09,192
لَئِنْ أُخْرِجْتُمْ لَنَخْرُجَنَّ مَعَكُمْ وَلَا نُطِيعُ فِيكُمْ أَحَدًا أَبَدًا

634
00:45:09,589 --> 00:45:18,577
وَإِنْ قُوتِلْتُمْ لَنَنْصُرَنَّكُمْ وَاللَّهُ يَشْهَدُ إِنَّهُمْ لَكَاذِبُونَ۝

635
00:45:19,297 --> 00:45:31,738
لَئِنْ أُخْرِجُوا لَا يَخْرُجُونَ مَعَهُمْ وَلَئِنْ قُوتِلُوا لَا يَنْصُرُونَهُمْ وَلَئِنْ نَصَرُوهُمْ لَيُوَلُّنَّ الْأَدْبَارَ

636
00:45:32,317 --> 00:45:40,764
وَلَئِنْ نَصَرُوهُمْ لَيُوَلُّنَّ الْأَدْبَارَ ثُمَّ لَا يُنْصَرُونَ۝

637
00:45:41,470 --> 00:45:46,290
Have you not considered, those who practice hypocrisy

638
00:45:46,823 --> 00:45:49,613
saying to their brothers, meaning the Jews,

639
00:45:49,653 --> 00:45:52,389
 who have disbelieved among the People of the Scripture.

640
00:45:53,013 --> 00:45:56,238
If you are expelled, we will surely leave with you

641
00:45:56,658 --> 00:45:59,856
and we will not obey in regard to you anyone, ever.

642
00:46:00,767 --> 00:46:06,214
And if you are fought we will surely aid you, but Allah testifies that they are liars.

643
00:46:07,204 --> 00:46:09,960
If they are expelled, they will not leave with them.

644
00:46:10,277 --> 00:46:13,206
And if they are fought, they will not aid them.

645
00:46:13,523 --> 00:46:19,274
And even if they should aid them they will surely turn their backs, then thereafter they will not be aided.

646
00:46:20,098 --> 00:46:25,157
These Munafiqoon(منافقون) are just talk, but they're empty they're worthless.

647
00:46:25,685 --> 00:46:27,997
They promised the Jews that they will stand with them

648
00:46:28,070 --> 00:46:29,935
if they are fought against, they will fight with them,

649
00:46:30,038 --> 00:46:31,679
if they're expelled, they're going to leave with them.

650
00:46:31,946 --> 00:46:33,888
None of this happened it was all lies.

651
00:46:35,161 --> 00:46:38,645
And Allah عَزّوجَلّ is revealing to us here some of the characteristics of Munafiqoon(منافقون).

652
00:46:38,693 --> 00:46:42,351
 Therefore we shouldn't be afraid of Al-Munafiqoon(منافقون).

653
00:46:42,407 --> 00:46:44,871
 There are Munafiqoon(منافقون) in the Ummah(أمة), they're very loud.

654
00:46:45,459 --> 00:46:49,839
They talk a lot and they threatened a lot, but all of it is empty talk.

655
00:46:50,418 --> 00:46:55,003
So the Muslims should not be threatened by these type of people

656
00:46:55,427 --> 00:46:57,074
and they deceived Al-Yahood(اليهود).

657
00:46:57,454 --> 00:47:00,206
The Yahood(اليهود) were waiting for help to come from Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن اُبَيئ)

658
00:47:00,250 --> 00:47:01,282
and none of it, showed up.

659
00:47:02,016 --> 00:47:04,606
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says even, if they help them they would have lost

660
00:47:04,773 --> 00:47:06,337
it wouldn't have made a difference anyway.

661
00:47:07,643 --> 00:47:09,044
Allahعَزّوجَلّ then says,

662
00:47:09,478 --> 00:47:15,938
لَأَنْتُمْ أَشَدُّ رَهْبَةً فِي صُدُورِهِمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ

663
00:47:16,850 --> 00:47:21,855
ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ۝

664
00:47:23,057 --> 00:47:32,345
لَا يُقَاتِلُونَكُمْ جَمِيعًا إِلَّا فِي قُرًى مُحَصَّنَةٍ أَوْ مِنْ وَرَاءِ جُدُرٍ

665
00:47:32,956 --> 00:47:36,251
بَأْسُهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ شَدِيدٌ

666
00:47:36,819 --> 00:47:41,577
تَحْسَبُهُمْ جَمِيعًا وَقُلُوبُهُمْ شَتَّىٰ

667
00:47:42,065 --> 00:47:47,176
ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَا يَعْقِلُونَ۝

668
00:47:48,205 --> 00:47:52,968
You believers are more fearful within their hearts from Allah,

669
00:47:53,003 --> 00:47:54,722
they fear you more then they fear Allah,

670
00:47:55,213 --> 00:47:58,973
you believers, and this is talking about all of Al-Kuffar(الكفار), not only Munafiqeen(منافقين),

671
00:47:59,025 --> 00:48:00,814
Al-Munafiqeen(منافقين), Al-Yahood(اليهود) all of the Kuffar(كفار).

672
00:48:01,137 --> 00:48:05,281
You believers are more fearful within their breasts, than Allah.

673
00:48:06,055 --> 00:48:08,834
This is because they are people, who do not understand.

674
00:48:10,632 --> 00:48:16,913
They will not fight you all, except within fortified cities or from behind walls

675
00:48:17,452 --> 00:48:22,959
and here Allahعَزّوجَلّ is disclosing to us this quality of Al-Kuffar(الكفار).

676
00:48:23,667 --> 00:48:27,748
They are not going to fight Muslims unless they are well fortified.

677
00:48:28,725 --> 00:48:34,360
Subhan Allah(سبحان الله) this fear of Al-Kuffar(الكفار) translates itself in two different forms.

678
00:48:35,293 --> 00:48:38,590
In the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ it was these fortresses

679
00:48:38,946 --> 00:48:43,933
in the time of crusades, it manifested itself in architectural wonders,

680
00:48:44,386 --> 00:48:45,815
in the land of Ash-sham(الشام),

681
00:48:46,108 --> 00:48:50,914
 the most beautiful works of architecture are the castles of the Crusaders.

682
00:48:52,154 --> 00:48:54,567
Yes it is wonderful work of architecture,

683
00:48:54,607 --> 00:48:59,271
but it's also reflects the fear that they had from the soldiers of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

684
00:48:59,549 --> 00:49:03,628
Salah-Ud-Din(صلاح الدين) wasn't building all of these castles, these castles were built by the Crusaders.

685
00:49:04,220 --> 00:49:07,470
And today the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ will not fight the Muslims

686
00:49:07,510 --> 00:49:09,085
except if they're well fortified.

687
00:49:09,125 --> 00:49:12,018
Look at this wall, that is now built in Falastine(فلسطين).

688
00:49:12,728 --> 00:49:14,144
That's a reflection of the fear.

689
00:49:14,383 --> 00:49:18,310
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) that wall is a fulfillment of this Ayah(آية) of Qur'an.

690
00:49:19,195 --> 00:49:21,282
They will not fight except from behind the wall

691
00:49:21,402 --> 00:49:24,277
or from a well protected cockpit in a plane

692
00:49:24,487 --> 00:49:26,618
or from the bowels of a ship

693
00:49:27,366 --> 00:49:31,890
but they do not have a courage to come out and fight like the the children of Al-Intifaadha(الانتفاضة)

694
00:49:32,689 --> 00:49:35,364
 out there in the open, fighting for Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

695
00:49:36,415 --> 00:49:40,878
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: Their violence among themselves is severe.

696
00:49:42,318 --> 00:49:46,887
This is to tell the Muslims that even though they gang up against you

697
00:49:47,270 --> 00:49:48,893
they come together and fight you.

698
00:49:49,858 --> 00:49:53,648
But their hearts are different, and they have hatred among themselves.

699
00:49:54,428 --> 00:49:56,421
Look at what the kuffar(كفار) do to each other.

700
00:49:57,008 --> 00:50:01,874
In World War One, you have 10 million killed in World War Two 50 million.

701
00:50:02,818 --> 00:50:06,278
Look at the wars that happened, among the European nations

702
00:50:06,342 --> 00:50:10,367
look at the wars in Africa look at wars in all over the world.

703
00:50:10,787 --> 00:50:13,494
So, don't think that the kuffar(كفار) are all one.

704
00:50:14,040 --> 00:50:15,958
No, they have differences among themselves

705
00:50:15,998 --> 00:50:19,843
but when it comes to Islam, Yes, they unify and they come and fight together,

706
00:50:20,261 --> 00:50:24,000
 but we should realize that they have differences among themselves too.

707
00:50:24,663 --> 00:50:25,695
وَقُلُوبُهُمْ شَتَّىٰ

708
00:50:26,626 --> 00:50:29,322
Their violence among themselves is severe.

709
00:50:30,050 --> 00:50:34,443
Again World War One and World War Two are an example of that.

710
00:50:34,744 --> 00:50:37,527
You think they are together but their hearts are diverse.

711
00:50:38,403 --> 00:50:40,843
That is because they are people who do not reason.

712
00:50:41,095 --> 00:50:47,512
لَأَنْتُمْ أَشَدُّ رَهْبَةً فِي صُدُورِهِمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ

713
00:50:48,382 --> 00:50:53,477
ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ۝

714
00:50:54,619 --> 00:51:03,891
 لَا يُقَاتِلُونَكُمْ جَمِيعًا إِلَّا فِي قُرًى مُحَصَّنَةٍ أَوْ مِنْ وَرَاءِ جُدُرٍ ۚ

715
00:51:04,569 --> 00:51:07,800
بَأْسُهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ شَدِيدٌ

716
00:51:08,348 --> 00:51:13,093
تَحْسَبُهُمْ جَمِيعًا وَقُلُوبُهُمْ شَتَّىٰ

717
00:51:13,680 --> 00:51:18,673
ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَا يَعْقِلُونَ۝

718
00:51:19,439 --> 00:51:22,149
There is like the example of those, shortly before them,

719
00:51:22,174 --> 00:51:24,734
they tasted the bad consequences of their affair

720
00:51:25,070 --> 00:51:26,887
and they will have a painful punishment.

721
00:51:26,927 --> 00:51:28,375
This is talking about Bannu Qainuqah(بنوقينقاع)

722
00:51:28,923 --> 00:51:30,937
who were driven out of Madina before Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير),

723
00:51:30,984 --> 00:51:36,023
Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير) should have taken heed of what happened to Bannu Qainuqah(بنوقينقاع).

724
00:51:36,964 --> 00:51:41,466
These are some lessons from the Ayaat(آيات) of Surat(سورة) An-Nadhir(النضير).

725
00:51:41,498 --> 00:51:47,636
 We have read the Aayat(آيات), up until about verse 16 or 15 if you want to go back and check them.

726
00:51:48,302 --> 00:51:53,670
The Arabs of Madina, in the time of Jahiliyyah(جاهليه)

727
00:51:54,279 --> 00:52:00,914
They had the superstition that if they have children and they keep on dying.

728
00:52:01,183 --> 00:52:04,294
So the mother will have a child and then the child will die,

729
00:52:04,381 --> 00:52:07,262
she will have the second child and that child will die,

730
00:52:07,700 --> 00:52:13,262
they had the superstition that if you make a vow that your next child will be a Jew,

731
00:52:13,867 --> 00:52:15,209
then the child will live,

732
00:52:15,670 --> 00:52:20,075
this was some superstition that existed among the people of Madina, before Islam.

733
00:52:20,537 --> 00:52:25,046
Because of this, they had children, who were growing up with Al-Yahood(اليهود)

734
00:52:25,725 --> 00:52:28,009
as a fulfillment of those vows.

735
00:52:28,524 --> 00:52:33,332
So now, when the Jews of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير) are going to be driven out,

736
00:52:33,372 --> 00:52:35,070
 they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

737
00:52:35,703 --> 00:52:38,690
We have some of our sons and some of our brothers are with them.

738
00:52:39,063 --> 00:52:40,111
What should we do?

739
00:52:40,574 --> 00:52:45,193
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not answer back, until an Ayah(آية) in Qur'an was revealed,

740
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:47,224
And that Ayah(آية) was:

741
00:52:47,249 --> 00:52:51,124
 لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ ۖ قَدْ تَبَيَّنَ الرُّشْدُ مِنَ الْغَيِّ ۚ

742
00:52:51,435 --> 00:52:53,294
There is no compulsion in religion

743
00:52:53,334 --> 00:52:57,540
and you all know this verse, it's in Surat-Ul-Baqarah(سورة البقرة) there is no compulsion in religion.

744
00:52:58,054 --> 00:53:00,954
Path of good is clear on the path of evil is clear.

745
00:53:01,425 --> 00:53:03,830
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told them,

746
00:53:04,363 --> 00:53:06,298
This is a Sahih(صحيح) narration

747
00:53:06,609 --> 00:53:11,064
قَدْ خُيِّرَ أَصْحَابكُمْ , فَإِنْ اخْتَارُوكُمْ فَهُمْ مِنْكُمْ , وَإِنْ اخْتَارُوهُمْ فَهُمْ مِنْهُمْ

748
00:53:11,675 --> 00:53:14,969
Give these brothers and Sons of yours the choice,

749
00:53:15,457 --> 00:53:20,460
if they choose you, then they stay with you, if they choose to be with the Jews, then they leave with them.

750
00:53:21,370 --> 00:53:24,324
In other words, you cannot compel them, you cannot force them

751
00:53:25,209 --> 00:53:26,596
to stay behind and become Muslim,

752
00:53:27,123 --> 00:53:30,901
even though they are ethnically Arabs even though they are your own children.

753
00:53:31,588 --> 00:53:34,310
These issues are not about ethnicity

754
00:53:34,350 --> 00:53:37,002
and we talked about this issue of nationalism, and all of that.

755
00:53:37,319 --> 00:53:41,292
Islam doesn't recognize this, it is what is in your heart that's what counts.

756
00:53:42,044 --> 00:53:44,848
Islam is not against a particular race,

757
00:53:44,888 --> 00:53:50,358
whether that race is the Jewish race or the white race or any race.

758
00:53:50,641 --> 00:53:54,252
Islam is not against any particular race Islam is a religion for everyone.

759
00:53:54,680 --> 00:53:55,954
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

760
00:53:55,994 --> 00:53:59,485
Allahعَزّوجَلّ does not look at your forms or the color of your skin.

761
00:53:59,726 --> 00:54:01,529
Allahعَزّوجَلّ looks at your hearts.

762
00:54:01,771 --> 00:54:06,266
So, these children of yours even though they are part of your families,

763
00:54:06,883 --> 00:54:08,675
if they choose you, then they are Muslim

764
00:54:08,715 --> 00:54:11,677
 if they choose the Yahood(يهود), then they have to leave with them,

765
00:54:11,907 --> 00:54:15,407
and you cannot force them otherwise to become Muslim.

766
00:54:15,963 --> 00:54:20,950
And this is the reason for the revelation of this Ayah(آية) that we all know in Surat-Ul-Baqarah(سورة البقرة),

767
00:54:21,220 --> 00:54:22,119
  لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ ۖ

768
00:54:22,428 --> 00:54:26,682
Also alcohol was banned, during the siege of Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير),

769
00:54:26,722 --> 00:54:30,873
 that's when the Ayah(آية) prohibiting alcohol was revealed,

770
00:54:31,192 --> 00:54:37,229
 and you know that the prohibition of alcohol occurred in four stages, this was the final stage.

771
00:54:37,610 --> 00:54:40,770
So, it's pretty late and we were talking about the fourth year of Hijrah(هجرى).

772
00:54:41,110 --> 00:54:46,106
So, Muslims, continue drinking for 17 years.

773
00:54:46,891 --> 00:54:51,256
It wasn't until the last six years of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ that alcohol was banned.

774
00:54:52,060 --> 00:54:55,782
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

